+  // and dispatching the "input"/"change" pair from script, so two things a
+  // real interaction always does are missing: the control is never marked
+  // user-interacted, and no user gesture is registered on the document. A
+  // dropdown <select> also loses the mouse events the parent process sends to
+  // the chosen <option>. Add them back here, for the dispatches that reach
+  // this function directly rather than through
+  // nsContentUtils::DispatchInputEvent, which does both itself. System callers
+  // count because Juggler's parent-built events (_setFileInputFiles) are still
+  // untrusted until DispatchDOMEvent promotes them, further down.
